ared to clean his prize with steady, practiced hands. The blade sliced through the thick skin with a satisfying hiss, releasing a cloud of red blood that stained the white deck. Miller wiped the blade on his trousers, the familiar ritual grounding him as he began to gut the fish with efficient, rhythmic strokes."
}

